            {"day": "Thu", "mins": 45, "topic": "ReAct and a tool-calling agent loop without frameworks",
             "learn": "ReAct = reason, act, observe until done; native tool calling replaces text parsing; loop guardrails: max steps, tool allow-list, argument validation, errors returned as observations, final-answer detection. Read: [ReAct paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.03629) (abstract and figure 1). Optional: [LLM Powered Autonomous Agents (Lilian Weng)](https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-06-23-agent/) (planning, tool use).",
             "do": "Write `agent.py` (about 80 lines, no framework): call the model with tool schemas, execute requested tools, append results, stop on a final answer or after 6 steps. Tools: `search_jobs(query)` over local JSON, `get_skill_gap(job_id)`, `calc(expression)` with safe parsing. Done when: a 3-step task (find Java + AI jobs in Bengaluru, then my gap for the best one) completes with a printed trace."},
            {"day": "Fri", "mins": 45, "topic": "Agent memory: short-term, long-term, context engineering",
             "learn": "Short-term memory (message window, running summary, trimming) vs long-term memory (profile facts, episodic logs, vector recall); context engineering: give the model the smallest high-signal context. Read: [Effective context engineering for AI agents (Anthropic)](https://www.anthropic.com/research/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents). Optional: [LangChain memory concepts](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/concepts/memory).",
             "do": "Add a message window plus running summary, and a long-term `profile.json` the agent reads and updates through `remember(fact)` and `recall(topic)` tools (simple embedding search). Set a token budget per turn. Done when: a fresh session recalls your target role and skills, and prompts stay under your budget."},
