            {"day": "Fri", "mins": 45, "topic": "Serving: vLLM, KV cache, continuous batching, model choice",
             "learn": "Prefill vs decode, KV-cache memory, continuous batching, PagedAttention, throughput vs latency; choose models by your own task evals first, then leaderboards (LMArena, Artificial Analysis), license, price per 1M tokens and latency. Read: [vLLM and PagedAttention](https://blog.vllm.ai/2023/06/20/vllm.html). Optional: [KV caching explained](https://huggingface.co/blog/not-lain/kv-caching).",
             "do": "Write `serving_notes.md`: prefill vs decode, the KV-cache size formula (2 x layers x kv_heads x head_dim x tokens x bytes) with an estimate for an 8B model at 8k context, and local-vs-API trade-offs for DocuMind. Then commit a `bench.py` skeleton that runs one golden question through a given `llmkit` provider and prints latency. Done when: the notes are committed and `bench.py` works for one model."},
